message: "If you use this work, please cite the Preprints.org version (peer-reviewed venue pending)."
title: "LRLS-v1.1: A Specification and Reference Simulation for Dual-Agent Exploration-Exploitation Under Hard Constraints"
abstract: >-
  LRLS role-separates the exploration-exploitation trade-off into two heterogeneous
  agent populations plus a scheduler: a high-entropy explorer proposes candidate
  habitats, a constraint-aware refiner promotes them into verified feasible solutions
  through bounded projection, and a scheduler allocates budget from global state. The
  work ships an executable specification, a dependency-free deterministic reference
  implementation, and a five-seed budget-matched comparison against four baselines.
  The headline finding is a negative one for speed - random search and a single-pool
  ablation reach 99% of the optimum 1.3-2.9x faster - while role separation reaches
  the quality threshold with zero hazard-zone evaluations in every seed.
